---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Android, Love Desire"
  description="Download the signed Android APK. Same features as iOS, no Google Play."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pt-20 pb-12 text-center">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-muted font-bold mb-3">Android</p>
    <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-6xl leading-tight text-burgundy">
      Sideload,<br />
      <em class="font-normal">no Play Store</em>.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-burgundy/80 mt-6 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
      Love Desire on Android is a direct APK download. The same app iPhone users get, nothing stripped out to fit Play Store rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Download -->
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16">
    <div class="bg-burgundy text-cream rounded-3xl p-8 md:p-12 text-center flex flex-col items-center gap-6">
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.35em] text-cream/60 font-bold">Latest release</p>
      <h2 class="font-heading text-4xl md:text-5xl text-cream">
        Love Desire v1.0.0
      </h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-cream/70 italic">Coming with launch. Check back soon.</p>
      <button
        type="button"
        disabled
        aria-disabled="true"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-cream text-burgundy px-8 py-4 rounded-full font-body font-bold text-sm shadow-md opacity-50 cursor-not-allowed"
      >
        <span>▾</span>
        <span>Download APK (~ 50 MB)</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Install instructions -->
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16">
    <h2 class="font-heading text-3xl text-burgundy mb-6">How to install</h2>
    <ol class="flex flex-col gap-6 text-burgundy/85 leading-relaxed">
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-blush rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-burgundy">1</span>
        <div>
          <p class="font-heading text-lg text-burgundy mb-1">Download the APK</p>
          <p class="text-sm">Tap the download button above from your Android device.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-blush rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-burgundy">2</span>
        <div>
          <p class="font-heading text-lg text-burgundy mb-1">Allow install from this source</p>
          <p class="text-sm">Your browser will warn you. Open the downloaded APK, Android asks you to allow 'Install unknown apps' for your browser. Grant it, then tap Install.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-blush rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-burgundy">3</span>
        <div>
          <p class="font-heading text-lg text-burgundy mb-1">Open Love Desire</p>
          <p class="text-sm">The app appears in your launcher like any other. Sign up or sign in, share your invite code with your partner, and you're paired.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="flex gap-4">
        <span class="flex-none w-8 h-8 bg-blush rounded-full flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-burgundy">4</span>
        <div>
          <p class="font-heading text-lg text-burgundy mb-1">Updates</p>
          <p class="text-sm">The app checks this page on launch and prompts you when a new version is available. One tap re-downloads the newest APK.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <!-- Why not Play Store -->
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">
    <div class="border-l-4 border-rose pl-6 py-2 flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h3 class="font-heading text-2xl text-burgundy">Why not on Google Play?</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-burgundy/80 leading-relaxed">
        Google Play's policies for adult content are stricter than Apple's. Shipping there would require a sanitized version with the Spicy tier removed, a different app for Android users. We'd rather ship one app for everyone. The Spicy tier and everything else, intact.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Security note -->
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-20">
    <div class="bg-blush rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h3 class="font-heading text-xl text-burgundy">About sideloading</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-burgundy/80 leading-relaxed">
        Sideloading an APK from an unknown source is normal on Android but you should always know who you're downloading from. Our APKs are signed with a consistent developer key. Android verifies the signature matches on every update, and refuses to install a differently-signed APK claiming to be Love Desire. If you ever see a signature mismatch prompt, don't proceed and email us.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
